; ============================================================
; Star logo - hatch fill engraving on dark acrylic
; Generated by hand (no skill) - even-odd horizontal hatch fill
; ============================================================
; Target size      : 50 mm x 50 mm (SVG scaled 0.5x)
; Material         : Dark / black acrylic sheet
; Operation        : ENGRAVE FILL (not cut-through)
; Laser            : 20W diode
; Power (S)        : 350 / 1000  (~35% => ~7.0W effective)
; Engrave feed     : 2500 mm/min
; Travel feed      : 6000 mm/min
; Hatch spacing    : 0.15 mm
; Hatch direction   : bidirectional (zig-zag) to reduce travel
; Bounding box X   : 5.000 .. 49.000 mm
; Bounding box Y   : 5.000 .. 47.000 mm
; Workpiece origin : lower-left of star at (5, 5) mm
; ------------------------------------------------------------
; SAFETY NOTES:
;   1. Acrylic vapor is flammable - NEVER leave the machine unattended.
;   2. Dark acrylic engraves hot; keep a fire extinguisher nearby.
;   3. Verify focus and do a 10x10 mm test patch at the chosen power first.
;   4. Air assist ON to reduce flaming and improve edge quality.
;   5. Engrave with the protective film ON the acrylic to prevent smoke
;      staining the surface; peel after engraving.
;   6. Ensure exhaust/ventilation is running - acrylic fumes are harmful.
;   7. This is an ENGRAVE job: power is intentionally below cut-through.
;      Do NOT increase power without re-testing to avoid melting/warping.
; ============================================================

G90            ; absolute positioning
G21            ; units = millimeters
M4            ; dynamic laser power mode (PWM spindle)
S0            ; laser off initially
G0 X0 Y0      ; home / park

; --- Start engraving ---
G0 X26.955 Y5.075 F6000    ; travel to scan start
S350       ; laser on
G1 X27.045 F2500    ; engrave segment
S0            ; laser off at end of scan line
